#!/usr/bin/python3
"""spark-ai-ctl — privileged control wrapper for spark-ai-stack.

Installed root:root 0755 at /usr/local/sbin/spark-ai-ctl and invoked either
directly by root (systemd units) or via the NOPASSWD sudoers drop-in at
/etc/sudoers.d/spark-ai-stack (docs/CONTRACTS.md §5, §12 workstream B).

Security invariants (see docs/CONTRACTS.md §2 and docs/SECURITY.md):
  * This program refuses to run unless the effective UID is 0.
  * It NEVER reads user-writable files. The repository at
    /home/niyam-gb10/code/spark-ai-stack is UNTRUSTED input and is touched
    only by the `sync` verb, which reads it explicitly to copy it into
    /etc/spark-ai-stack (root-owned) after a human reviews a printed diff.
  * All other verbs consume ONLY root-owned files under /etc/spark-ai-stack,
    /var/lib/spark-ai-stack and /run/spark-ai-stack.
  * Every path this program writes to is a hardcoded constant. No verb
    accepts a free-form path, shell snippet, or environment passthrough.
  * subprocess is always invoked with an explicit argv list and shell=False.
  * Catalog-supplied CLI arguments and environment variables are validated
    against an explicit allow/deny policy before they are allowed to reach a
    rendered compose override (see validate_args_tokens / validate_environment).

Exit codes: 0 ok, 1 general/runtime error, 2 usage/refusal, 3 catalog content
rejected as unsafe (backend-start / backend-stop / gateway-reload render path).
"""

